james-will-2.md:1: argue/readings: S2 is read 3 ways: james-will-2.logic.r1 has "gnostic → acts_good ∧ regret_good"; james-will-2.logic.r1.2 has "gnostic → ◇(acts_good ∧ regret_good)" and "◇(acts_good ∧ regret_good) → gnostic"; they differ when only "the necessary acts we erroneously regret are good", "our error in so regretting them is also good", "possibly, (the necessary acts we erroneously regret are good and our error in so regretting them is also good)" and "possibly, (the necessary acts we erroneously regret are good and our error in so regretting them is also good)" are true, which the first allows; james-will-2.logic.r1.3 has "acts_good ∧ regret_good → gnostic"
